            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alex"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This had a very nice flavour. After chilling in the fridge for awhile, though, mine was still completely liquid, not syrup at all. I made it exactly as the recipe stated but perhaps I measured my butter incorrectly or something. No matter, even though it was liquid I put it on my oatmeal pancakes and it tasted great! UPDATE: I also recently made this to put on Strawberry Vanilla Pancakes from this site and that was a great flavour combo! Was still very liquidy again, but not a big deal."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angie Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so yummy and fast. I made the recipe to feed 8 people so I did 2 tablespoons butter and milk, 1 Tablespoon vanilla, and 3 Tablespoons Honey and then followed the directions. I will be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-19T09:24:39.013Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I upped this recipe to four servings. I used buttermilk instead of regular milk. That was the only change I made. We had this over Herman pancakes and it was so good--though it had a LOT of vanilla. Quadrupled, it was two tablespoons and two teaspoons of vanilla! I'd like to make this again cutting back a bit on the vanilla and with a touch of cinnamon. Very simple and a good fill in for when you're out of pancake syrup.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-13T04:37:59.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jesus is Lord and Savior"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent recipe. Of course you will have to adjust it to your liking like any other recipe. However I utilized the ingredients asked for and did as the recipe asked. The only thing I did that was DIFFERENT was not mix everything up once the honey and butter was done in the microwave melting. Instead I poured a little bit of the milk and vanilla (mixed up already) into the honey and butter. \nI did not feel the need to let it sit in the refrigerator. It was great this way. Of course I through some of the milk and vanilla mix away because I only wanted to use a little bit which kept it from being so watery. Such a lovely taste. Thank you so much.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-11T10:03:26.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this due to not having any maple syrup, it was really good !! . I doubled recipe. I used our stove top and put the honey in plus vanilla let that honey reduce its thickness then added the milk and butter .. I set aside and it thickens up after letting it cool down .. Turned out great .. Light taste . Just made some Ragluar pancakes",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-23T17:53:59.807Z"
          },
          {
